      "updated": 1795162935509,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "app.js registers the error middleware. Consider this ordering:\n\na) A request to GET /api/unknown is made. Which middleware\n    handles it, and what does the client receive?\nb) Where should the 404 handler go, and why does order matter?\nc) In production you do not want err.stack sent to clients.\n    Update errorMiddleware to include stack only when\n    NODE_ENV !== 'production'.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "app.js registers the error middleware. Consider this ordering:\n\na) A request to GET /api/unknown is made. Which middleware\n    handles it, and what does the client receive?\nb) Where should the 404 handler go, and why does order matter?\nc) In production you do not want err.stack sent to clients.\n    Update errorMiddleware to include stack only when\n    NODE_ENV !== 'production'.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aG"
    },
